  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      205.75,
      195.33,
      391.76,
      252.97
    ],
    "text": "(4) The trial Judge may refer to the RecorderJudge any matter of a procedural nature arisingin the course of the proceedings instituted inthat court after the stage referred to insubsection (3).",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      205.75,
      263.85,
      391.77,
      321.49
    ],
    "text": "(5) The Recorder Judge may, with theconcurrence of the trial Judge, submit fordetermination by the trial Judge any matterwhich may otherwise have been properly dealtwith by him.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      217.75,
      332.37,
      340.75,
      342.37
    ],
    "text": "(6) The Recorder Judge shall\u2013",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      232.87,
      352.19,
      391.75,
      386.05
    ],
    "text": "(a)sit separately and exercise allthe powers vested in him bysubsection (3);",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      232.87,
      395.87,
      391.76,
      465.49
    ],
    "text": "(b)have the power to do all such actsconnected with or incidental orancillary to the exercise of thepowers referred to in subsection (3)including the maintenance of theJournals of the Court; and",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      233.47,
      475.31,
      391.76,
      616.21
    ],
    "text": "(c)exercise the powers in relation topre-trial conferences as specified insection 195A of the Code ofCriminal Procedure Act, No. 15 of1979 only in respect of matterswhere the High Court exercisescriminal jurisdiction in terms ofsection 9 and shall not exercise thepowers in respect of matters wherethe High Court is called upon toexercise appellate, revisionary orwrit jurisdiction.\u201d.",
    "fonts": [
      "Times-Italic",
      "Times-Roman"
    ],
    "sizes": [
      7.0,
      10.0
    ]
  },
  {
    "page_number": 3,
    "bbox": [
      151.75,
      629.99,
      391.75,
      651.97
    ],
    "text": "3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.",
